# Session cases

When jagt may send a session each step of `session-brief.md.dist`. Copy this file to `session-cases.md` to edit a
case; a case your copy lacks is read from here. A step at a status no case names is not sent: it is written to
`misses.jsonl` beside `state.json` instead.

Each case: `step:` a brief step · `at:` the task's statuses, `any` or `any but <statuses>` · `by:` jagt, master or
human, who sets it off · one line saying what the case is.

## start

step: start
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
A session starts in the task's worktree.

## revive

step: revive
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
A session that went down is entered again.

## context

step: context
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
A worktree is briefed with the session's standing rules.

## plan-by-human

step: plan
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: human
You approved the plan, so the session starts on it.

## plan-by-master

step: plan
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the plan and it holds, so the session starts on it.

## plan-not-ready

step: plan-not-ready
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the plan and sends its findings back.

## plan-answered

step: plan-answered
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master answers the question a plan was handed back with.

## round-not-ready

step: round-not-ready
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the hand-back and sends its findings back.

## asked-human

step: asked-human
at: PLAN_PENDING, REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master asked you a question, and the session waits on the answer.

## answered

step: answered
at: any but PLAN_PENDING, SHIPPING, DEPLOY_CONFLICT, DONE
by: master
The Master answers a session's question.

## answered-under

step: answered-under
at: SHIPPING, DEPLOY_CONFLICT
by: master
The Master answers a session's question below the instruction it still works on.

## repo-by-human

step: repo
at: any but DONE
by: human
You added the repository the session asked for.

## repo-by-master

step: repo
at: any but DONE
by: master
The Master added the repository the session asked for.

## verify

step: verify
at: VERIFYING
by: jagt
The project's verification command failed on a hand-back.

## probes

step: probes
at: VERIFYING
by: jagt
An acceptance probe of the plan failed on a hand-back.

## ship-by-human

step: ship
at: IN_PROGRESS, VERIFYING, REVIEW_PENDING, SHIPPING, CI_POLLING, CI_FAILED, REVIEWED, DEPLOYED, REVERTED
by: human
You shipped the task, so the session commits, pushes and opens its requests.

## ship-by-master

step: ship
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the hand-back and shipped it.

## round-checks-polled

step: round-checks
at: any but CI_POLLING, REVIEWED, APPROVED, DONE
by: jagt
The poll read red checks on the task's request.

## round-checks-swept

step: round-checks
at: any but CI_POLLING, REVIEWED, APPROVED, DONE
by: human
Your sweep read red checks on the task's request.

## round-checks-done-polled

step: round-checks-done
at: any but CI_POLLING, REVIEWED, APPROVED, DONE
by: jagt
The poll read red checks and no open thread.

## round-checks-done-swept

step: round-checks-done
at: any but CI_POLLING, REVIEWED, APPROVED, DONE
by: human
Your sweep read red checks and no open thread.

## round-threads-polled

step: round-threads
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
The poll read open threads on the task's request.

## round-threads-swept

step: round-threads
at: any but DONE
by: human
Your sweep read open threads on the task's request.

## round-threads-done-polled

step: round-threads-done
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
The poll read open threads, which end the round.

## round-threads-done-swept

step: round-threads-done
at: any but DONE
by: human
Your sweep read open threads, which end the round.

## deploy

step: deploy
at: DEPLOYED
by: jagt
The task is live on the deploy branch, so the session checks it where it landed.

## conflict

step: conflict
at: DEPLOY_CONFLICT
by: jagt
A deploy conflicts, and the session resolves it in the deploy worktree.

## wake

step: wake
at: any but DONE
by: jagt
A usage limit has reset, so a stopped session goes on.
